    {
      "@id": "./",
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "additionalType": "Investigation",
      "identifier": "7743f5cf-dafe-4193-bd84-d80dcf1c3405",
      "creator": {
        "@id": "#Person_Kevin_Urbasch"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-09-30T08:01:00Z",
      "description": "This dataset provides gridded crop presence information for Germany as yearly GeoTIFFs (1 km resolution) with one TIFF per year, crops represented by the bands.  A cell value of 1 represents crop cultivation in for that raster cell. Raster information is the result of aggregating field-based, vectorised crop areas to the 1 km raster resolution. Crop presence is recorded when crops cover at least 25% of a pixel, meaning at least 25 hectares within that pixel. This threshold-approach determines suitable pixels rather than deterministic crop cover information and might result in more than one crop being present per pixel. Missing crops in a given year (`CA`, `ON` after 2023) are represented as bands filled with `NA` values to ensure a consistent structure across time.",
